# Compiled executables on Linux have no extension (nvcc -o gemm), so instead
# of listing artifact types, ignore everything and whitelist source files.
# A new file type only gets tracked once it's added here -- that's the trade.
*

# directories must be un-ignored for the rules below to reach into them
!*/

# sources and headers
!*.cu
!*.cuh
!*.c
!*.cpp
!*.h
!*.hpp

# project files
!README.md
!*.md
!.gitignore
!.clangd
!Makefile
!CMakeLists.txt

# still ignore nvcc/profiler intermediates even if a rule above matches them
*.o
*.ptx
*.cubin
*.fatbin
*.nsys-rep
*.ncu-rep
.claude/
